%
(DMC2 X PROBE-OFFSET: SELECTED CONTACT INPUT TO FIXED PUCK)
(Authorized values: -X 40.00 mm maximum at 0.10 mm/s.)
(After IN1 contact is durably recorded: +X 1.00 mm at 0.10 mm/s.)
(No Y, Z, or spindle command is present.)

#<maximum_travel_mm> = 40.00
#<approach_feed_mm_min> = 6.00
#<backoff_distance_mm> = 1.00
#<backoff_feed_mm_min> = 6.00

G21 G91 G94

(Start with the existing OUT5 contact-test power path off.)
M65 P0
M66 P1 L4 Q1.0
o<dmc2_x_probe_initial_power_off> if [#5399 LT 0]
    (DEBUG,DMC2 X PROBE REFUSED: OUT5 gate did not report off)
    G90
    M2
o<dmc2_x_probe_initial_power_off> endif

(Enable OUT5 only while this LinuxCNC program is running.)
M64 P0
M66 P1 L3 Q1.0
o<dmc2_x_probe_power_on> if [#5399 LT 0]
    M65 P0
    (DEBUG,DMC2 X PROBE REFUSED: OUT5 gate did not report on)
    G90
    M2
o<dmc2_x_probe_power_on> endif

(The selected contact input must be open before movement.)
o<dmc2_x_probe_initial_open> if [#<_hal[motion.probe-input]> NE 0]
    M65 P0
    (DEBUG,DMC2 X PROBE REFUSED: selected contact input is already active)
    G90
    M2
o<dmc2_x_probe_initial_open> endif

(Open the durable capture before motion. LinuxCNC writes the accepted probe)
(point, and the file is closed before any backoff can begin.)
(PROBEOPEN /home/kit/linuxcnc_dmc2/var/log/linuxcnc/probe-offset-x-capture.txt)

(Exactly -X, maximum 40.00 mm, at 6.00 mm/min = 0.10 mm/s.)
G38.2 X[-#<maximum_travel_mm>] F#<approach_feed_mm_min>
#<probe_contact_machine_x> = #5061
(PROBECLOSE)
(DEBUG,DMC2 X PROBE CONTACT: X = #<probe_contact_machine_x> mm)

(Exactly +X 1.00 mm at 6.00 mm/min = 0.10 mm/s.)
G1 X#<backoff_distance_mm> F#<backoff_feed_mm_min>
#<backoff_machine_x> = #<_abs_x>

(Remove contact-test power after the requested backoff.)
M65 P0
M66 P1 L4 Q1.0
o<dmc2_x_probe_final_power_off> if [#5399 LT 0]
    (DEBUG,DMC2 X PROBE WARNING: OUT5 gate did not report off after backoff)
o<dmc2_x_probe_final_power_off> endif

G90
(DEBUG,DMC2 X PROBE BACKOFF COMPLETE: machine X = #<backoff_machine_x> mm)
M2
%
